    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **262 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI extended the business-day rule for owner registration dates to skip public holidays in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n1. **Added a fixed public-holiday set** \u2014 a `PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS` constant holding the five listed dates: `2026-01-01`, `2026-01-26`, `2026-04-25`, `2026-12-25`, `2026-12-28`.\n\n2. **Updated `toBusinessDay(...)`** \u2014 the roll-forward loop now advances the date by one day not only when it lands on a Saturday or Sunday, but also when it lands on a listed public holiday, continuing until it reaches a non-holiday weekday. This naturally handles chained cases (e.g. a holiday immediately followed by a weekend).\n\nThe change flows automatically through the two callers that already use `toBusinessDay` \u2014 the effective registration date computed on create, and the `ownersCreatedOn` daily-count/bulk-signup logic \u2014 so both consistently observe the holiday-adjusted date. The implementation matches the holiday list and logic already encoded in the acceptance test's `AcceptanceBase.toBusinessDay`.",
